
== the largest and smallest values (the mantissa is 2^90 - 1 at most) ==
1237940039285380274899124223d (max mantissa)         1237940039285380274899124223
-1237940039285380274899124223d                       -1237940039285380274899124223
12379400392853802748991242.23d (scale 2)             12379400392853802748991242.23
0.1237940039285380274899124223d (scale 28)           0.1237940039285380274899124223
0.0000000000000000000000000001d (smallest step)      0.0000000000000000000000000001
9223372036854775807d (the old 64-bit limit)          9223372036854775807
any 27 digit number fits                             999999999999999999999999999

== literals that do not fit are syntax errors ==
return 1237940039285380274899124224d                 Decimal literal is out of range
return 9999999999999999999999999999d                 Decimal literal is out of range
return 1e28d                                         Decimal literal is out of range
return 1e30d                                         Decimal literal is out of range
return 0.00000000000000000000000000001d              Decimal literal is out of range
return 1e-29d                                        Decimal literal is out of range
return 1.2.3d                                        Malformed decimal
return 1ed                                           Malformed decimal

== a result with too many digits is rounded, the scale drops ==
12379400392853802748991242.23d + 0.01d               12379400392853802748991242.2
12379400392853802748991242.23d + 0.001d              12379400392853802748991242.23
12379400392853802748991242.23d + 0.1d                12379400392853802748991242.3
0.1234567890123456789d * 1d                          0.1234567890123456789
0.1234567890123456789d * 0.1234567890123456789d      0.0152415787532388367501905200
9223372036854775.807d * 1.5d                         13835058055282163.7105
1d / 3d                                              0.333333333333333333333333333
1d / 3d * 3d                                         0.999999999999999999999999999

== the scale is capped at 28 ==
0.0000000000000001d * 0.0000000000000001d            0.0000000000000000000000000000
0.00000000000000000001d * 0.00000000000000000001d    0.0000000000000000000000000000
0.0000000000000001d * 0.000000000000000001d          0.0000000000000000000000000000
1d / 9223372036854775807d                            0.0000000000000000001084202172
decimal.create(1e-29)                                0.0000000000000000000000000000

== overflow: a value that does not fit even at scale 0 ==
1237940039285380274899124223d + 1d                   error: decimal overflow
1237940039285380274899124223d * 2d                   error: decimal overflow
1237940039285380274899124223d * 10d                  error: decimal overflow
-1237940039285380274899124223d - 1d                  error: decimal overflow
100000000000000d * 100000000000000d                  error: decimal overflow
decimal.mul(10000000000000d, 100000000000000d) (10^27 fits) 1000000000000000000000000000
1000000000000d * 1000000000000d (fits)               1000000000000000000000000
1237940039285380274899124222d + 1d (fits)            1237940039285380274899124223
a fraction can round away (…223.4 is …223)       1237940039285380274899124223
but the integer part never does (…223.6 would need …224) error: decimal overflow

== but digits can be traded for range ==
123794003928538027489912422.3d + 0.1d                123794003928538027489912422
123794003928538027489912422.3d * 10d                 1237940039285380274899124223
123794003928538027489912422.3d * 100d                error: decimal overflow

== remainder aligns both operands to a common scale first (256 bits, so it does not overflow) ==
1d % 0.0000000000000000001d                          0.0000000000000000000
1237940039285380274899124223d % 0.0000000000000000000000001d 0.0000000000000000000000000
7d % 0.0000000000000000000000000003d                 0.0000000000000000000000000001

== what 90 bits are good for ==
largest amount with 2 decimals                       12379400392853802748991242.23
largest amount with 4 decimals                       123794003928538027489912.4223
largest amount with 8 decimals                       12379400392853802748.99124223
largest amount with 18 decimals                      1237940039.285380274899124223
one million tokens with 18 decimals                  1000000.000000000000000000
plus one wei                                         1000000.000000000000000001
a billion tokens still fits                          1000000000.000000000000000000
ten billion tokens does not (fromstring gives nil)   10000000000.00000000000000000
